<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pybba of Mercia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 600</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pybba was an early king of the Mercians around 600, known only from later royal genealogies. These make him the son of Creoda and the father of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/penda-of-mercia">Penda</a> and Eowa, and trace the line back to the legendary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/icel">Icel</a>. Nothing is recorded of his reign, and even his kingship rests on these late lists rather than contemporary evidence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pybba-of-mercia.jpg" alt="Pybba of Mercia" width="320" height="398" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Hel-hama · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Britain_peoples_circa_600.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
